<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>eu.wohlben</groupId>
        <artifactId>qits</artifactId>
        <version>2026.918.233419</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <!-- PUBLISHED COORDINATES, and they deliberately do not inherit the parent's. `eu.wohlben.qits:
         qits-*` is what every artifact this platform publishes is called (qits-auth-core,
         qits-db-core, qits-eventstream, qits-workspace-daemon-protocol), and this module joined
         them the day qits-projects started taking the `qits/project-agent` image version from a
         released dependency instead of a configuration entry — see ProjectAgentImage.

         THE COORDINATE IT LANDS ON IS THE ONE THE VENDORED COPY ALREADY OCCUPIES, and that is not
         an accident to be tidied up — it is the vendored module's own plan coming due.
         qits-projects-service's `projects-daemon-protocol/` is `eu.wohlben.qits:
         qits-projects-daemon-protocol` at ITS reactor's calver, and its pom says in as many words
         that "the day this artifact is published somewhere, deleting this module and adding a
         <dependency> is a one-line change with no source edits". That day is this one, and landing
         on the same groupId:artifactId is what makes it one line: the consumer deletes the module
         and the same two strings resolve from the registry instead of the reactor.

         Until that consumer release lands there are briefly two things called
         `eu.wohlben.qits:qits-projects-daemon-protocol` — this one at this repository's calver, that
         one at qits-projects' — which is harmless because they are different VERSIONS and because
         the consumer does not depend on the published one yet. It is also why the two must not sit
         in that state for long. -->
    <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
    <artifactId>qits-projects-daemon-protocol</artifactId>

    <!-- The projects-daemon control-plane wire contract: plain records + enums + the shared
         type/field-name constants, framework-free and dependency-free. Both ends depend on it so
         neither owns the protocol. No JSON library here on purpose: serialization lives on each
         side against whatever it already carries.

         IT CARRIES THE RELEASE'S OWN VERSION TOO ({@code ProjectAgentImage}), which is why it is
         the module that gets deployed rather than a second "pin" jar beside it: the thing a
         consumer must pin and the thing it must speak are the same release, and one artifact
         cannot ship half of that pair. -->

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <!-- FILTERING IS ON FOR THIS MODULE'S ONE RESOURCE AND NOTHING ELSE. The include/exclude
             pair is not belt-and-braces: filtering every resource would rewrite any future binary
             fixture that happens to contain `${`, and this module is the wire contract — a corrupt
             fixture here is a wrong assertion, not a build error. ProjectAgentImage refuses an
             unfiltered value, so switching this block off fails loudly rather than shipping the
             literal `${project.version}` as an image tag.

             THE DELIMITERS HERE ARE MAVEN'S DEFAULTS, `${...}`, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT. The
             sibling `projects-daemon/pom.xml` configures maven-resources-plugin with
             `<useDefaultDelimiters>false</useDefaultDelimiters>` and `@` only, so that Quarkus's
             own `${config.expression}` references in its application.properties survive filtering.
             That configuration is MODULE-LOCAL — it sits in that module's `<build><plugins>`, not
             in the parent's `<pluginManagement>`, which pins only quarkus/compiler/surefire — so
             none of it reaches here. If a delimiter override ever moves up to the parent, this
             module's resource must switch to `@project.version@` in the same edit; the test below
             is what catches a miss. -->
        <resources>
            <resource>
                <directory>src/main/resources</directory>
                <filtering>true</filtering>
                <includes>
                    <include>eu/wohlben/qits/projectsdaemon/protocol/project-agent-image.properties</include>
                </includes>
            </resource>
            <resource>
                <directory>src/main/resources</directory>
                <filtering>false</filtering>
                <excludes>
                    <exclude>eu/wohlben/qits/projectsdaemon/protocol/project-agent-image.properties</exclude>
                </excludes>
            </resource>
        </resources>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
